 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T12:59+08:00",
 "answer": "**I’d skip a strenuous outdoor workout in Jurong right now.** It’s currently raining and hot (about 31°C), and NEA’s forecast for **Saturday, 17 October** is PSI **150–230**—unhealthy to very unhealthy—with advice for healthy people to avoid prolonged or strenuous outdoor exertion. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))\n\nFor a short, light outing, check NEA’s **live 1-hour PM2.5 reading for the West** first; that’s the better guide for immediate activity. If it’s elevated, scale back; if it’s high, avoid strenuous exercise. If you’re older, pregnant, a child, or have heart or lung disease, take extra care and avoid outdoor activity as advised. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))",
